<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Guzmán Blanco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Guzmán Blanco was a Venezuelan general and statesman who dominated the country from 1870 to 1888 as president or through allies. A Liberal leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-war">Federal War</a>, he made primary education free and compulsory, introduced the bolívar as the currency, curbed the power of the Church and built railways and public works, remodelling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> in a French style. He grew immensely rich and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-guzman-blanco.jpg" alt="Antonio Guzmán Blanco" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martín Tovar y Tovar (1827 - 1902), restored version · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martin_Tovar_y_Tovar_20_restored.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
